# Stage 12 — the identifiers with nothing between the prefix and the word.
#
# The last GF family. Every earlier scan required a separator after the prefix
# (gform_, gform-, gf/), so bare gform and gfield were invisible to all of them.
# 118 identifiers, 3776 occurrences.
#
# Naming rule as given: where the f belongs to the following word, only the g
# changes — gform to kform, gfield to kfield, gsection to ksection. Where gf is
# the Gravity Forms abbreviation and the next letters start a new word, the
# whole gf becomes kdna — gfMultiFileUploader to kdnaMultiFileUploader.
#
# The riskiest single entry in the whole rename is gform, at 1173 occurrences:
# it is the JS namespace, so gform.applyFilters, gform.addAction and above all
# gform.initializeOnLoaded, which gates whether a form renders at all. It moves
# in one pass across PHP inline scripts and every bundle, or not at all.
#
# Bare gf is deliberately absent. It is the REST namespace in gf/v2 and in the
# $rest_prefix . 'gf/' check beside it, both public URLs, and renaming a bare
# token would take them with it. The two gf:json delimiters below are handled
# as whole strings instead, so the namespace cannot be caught by accident.
#
# The frozen database and option names are absent too: every one of them
# carries an underscore, and none is in this list.

gfield                             kfield
gform                              kform
gchoice                            kchoice
gsection                           ksection
gformFormat                        kformFormat
gresults                           kresults
